  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-lfaa",
      "text": "English | [中文](README.zh.md)\n\nA complete native DSH plugin project with independently owned business modules. Appearance, layout, cards, dialogs and motion are one capability group, not the definition of the whole plugin. This is a new project designed around DSH; it does not copy or migrate the old LFAA project."
    },
    {
      "section": "dsh-lfaa",
      "text": "DSH owns accounts, all AI execution, sessions, models, subagents, tool dispatch and approval. The plugin contributes its own business through public interfaces and keeps business data local when needed. No second harness, login or conversation store is introduced."
    },
    {
      "section": "dsh-lfaa",
      "text": "The three-column writing workspace manages novel projects and chapters, autosaves the selected chapter, and sends AI polish/continuation prompts through a selected DSH conversation. Results appear as suggestions and are applied only after a user action. Writing data is stored locally under the verified DSH account profile ID."
    },
    {
      "section": "Repository",
      "text": "```text\npackages/\n  dsh-lfaa/              Plugin composition and distribution manifest\n  dsh-lfaa-workspace/    Novel workspace, editor, Session tab, right pane, Settings\n  dsh-lfaa-appearance/   Appearance schema and reversible theme/motion projection\n\nPackage directories and manifest names use the `dsh-` prefix. Private implementation packages are bundled into one installable `dsh-lfaa` artifact; users do not install the development workspace."
    },
    {
      "section": "Develop",
      "text": "The DSH repository root is also an install facade: its manifest points to the committed `dist/packages/dsh-lfaa/` output, so GitHub installs do not need to run a build lifecycle script. The package ships both root entries and matching `dist/` compatibility entries for older DSH loaders. In DSH's Add Plugin dialog, enter the repository URL `https://github.com/yubboo/dsh-lfaa.git`; for a local install, run `pnpm run build` first and enter this repository's root directory. The GitHub push menu rebuilds the installable output before staging it. The build excludes private workspace dependencies, development source, test fixtures and user data. The package name `dsh-lfaa` works after the built distribution is published to npm. On Windows, run `publish-npm.bat` from the repository root: menu 6 safely pushes to GitHub `main`, requiring a commit message that starts with a new three-part source version; menu 7 builds, previews and publishes to the official npm registry after confirmation, and menus 1–5 provide package checks. The last pushed source version is read from GitHub commit history, with a local Git config fallback. The menu implementation is `scripts/publish-menu.ps1`; the batch la"
    },
    {
      "section": "Develop",
      "text": "Minecraft currently supports Paper and Fabric Host services and Agent operations, with a session workspace panel for distribution/version discovery, server create/install, status, start/stop, configuration, file inspection, console commands, backup/restore, and mod search/install. Fabric mods are searched through Modrinth by Minecraft version and installed only into a stopped Fabric instance; required dependencies are resolved recursively and downloaded files are checked against Modrinth SHA-512 metadata. Modpacks, Forge, NeoForge, and end-to-end acceptance in a real DSH Profile remain unfinished. The panel submits explicit requests into the active DSH conversation; the Agent inspects Java and may install an official Temurin runtime when needed, while downloads, writes, and process actions remain subject to DSH approval. The user must explicitly confirm Minecraft EULA acceptance. Paper downloads carry publisher SHA-256 metadata. Fabric's official HTTPS bootstrap endpoint does not publish the same checksum metadata, so the plugin records the downloaded file's local hash and validates its JAR format without claiming publisher-checksum verification."
    }
  ],
